 "summary": "The Rayleigh-formula definition via `f \u21a6 -dslope (deriv f) 0` is faithful to `j_l(x) = (-x)^l (1/x d/dx)^l (sin x/x)`, and the evenness of each iterate correctly licenses identifying it with `-(1/x)d/dx` off the origin and with the limiting value at it. I recomputed the closed forms, the origin values `1/(2l+1)\u203c`, both ladder relations, the second-derivative formula and the ODE against DLMF \u00a7\u00a710.49, 10.51, 10.52 and found no mismatch; whole-line statements that degenerate at `0` are documented and paired with non-degenerate origin lemmas.",
